/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c4565b1-69f9-5bcf-baa2-75d567dcc9de" :question/math-academy-id "q-102705" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y=1 \\\\ 2x-3y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dec4d8a-eb47-5a0e-8bc6-79e5c68ce845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311784} {:answer/id #uuid "6a00b159-494d-57f0-b2df-848c702a6c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311785} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7ebea2-6028-56f1-94f6-58c564514eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311786} {:answer/id #uuid "9ebd9aa1-0838-5623-8e6e-5cb815f79024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311787} {:answer/id #uuid "a24530fd-1240-5b73-957a-7bf1c97a3970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a00b159-494d-57f0-b2df-848c702a6c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311785} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ed1587-7f70-5901-935f-5fea3708eadb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "380e10d6-e728-562d-9721-3838f62a9783" :question/math-academy-id "q-102808" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3=y \\\\ 3y=4x+2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ -4x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c010b75-821c-58b3-afc9-00c0bf092020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347176} {:answer/id #uuid "0d33f3be-3f54-5335-bdb3-0bcd69118688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347177} {:answer/id #uuid "c00ee482-bf1f-5b49-903b-a43438da12f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347178} {:answer/id #uuid "c94f5b72-8f1c-52ff-8721-0636b25674ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347179} {:answer/id #uuid "4540b966-2966-5174-b7ea-f1a753ca4f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4540b966-2966-5174-b7ea-f1a753ca4f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347180} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b8138c2-031b-5275-a3f9-a7b36a06e3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b97b4d5-838b-5cc5-a6ea-8c327bb5d331" :question/math-academy-id "q-32141" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=7 \\\\ 8x+y=7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d0b7924-0d1f-5a68-a3eb-f25c3a37982c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347182} {:answer/id #uuid "04aff1b5-5e89-5580-8fcb-20124c6a053e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347183} {:answer/id #uuid "6076d752-68c4-5c39-abf8-438e0bff111a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347184} {:answer/id #uuid "47b83c08-ba68-5633-926d-36dc4338af67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347185} {:answer/id #uuid "da3819a6-98ba-562d-b2dd-e051795c5af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04aff1b5-5e89-5580-8fcb-20124c6a053e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347183} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aacc902-1c76-5d63-80c2-7563a9d8956a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7ea58d8-c912-5e16-b0bd-a3c96b9a8c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8857" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x=5y \\\\ x=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y=0 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "657d1d4e-1db1-5ed2-91b3-c51adf5dbe50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347188} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9b5840-5452-5034-ab41-46c9016587b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347189} {:answer/id #uuid "e8aa4411-a0fe-5307-802e-eb8550bd83e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347190} {:answer/id #uuid "ef78426b-71bb-5191-b761-8b34b7d07419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347191} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa1fe5c-4c55-5bf1-b4b3-6452f295acec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8aa4411-a0fe-5307-802e-eb8550bd83e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347190} :answer-field/id #uuid "e482e1be-97c7-5508-bf74-3600bb80e239" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c79bea22-6c3f-5522-b32f-6f5b851abe6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8858" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=0 \\\\ 3x-6y=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-6)-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
